  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Melt the butter with the olive oil in a wide pot over medium-high. Add the mushrooms in one layer and leave them alone for 5 minutes so they brown instead of steaming.",
      "timer_min": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir, add the onion, and cook for 5 minutes more, scraping the browned bits up from the bottom.",
      "timer_min": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the garlic and barley and toast, stirring, for 2 minutes - the grains should smell nutty.",
      "timer_min": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour in the water, add the salt, and bring to a boil, then cover and simmer gently for 25 minutes, until the barley is tender with a slight chew.",
      "timer_min": 25
    },
    {
      "text": "Off the heat, stir the sour cream through in two additions so it warms without splitting."
    },
    {
      "text": "Taste for salt and pepper, shower with the chives, and serve straight from the pot. Leftovers keep four days; loosen with a splash of water when reheating."
    }
  ],
